# Supabase Table Audit Columns

When creating or modifying SQL table definitions in `supabase/tables/`, every table must include these audit columns at the **end** of the column list unless explicitly instructed otherwise:

```sql
is_hidden BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
created_by UUID,
created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
modified_by UUID,
modified_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
```

## Rules

- Place audit columns last, after all domain columns
- Do not omit, rename, or reorder these columns unless the user explicitly says so
- Match types, nullability, and defaults exactly as shown
